<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Kindness Bags | The Ripple Effect Project</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Navigation -->
  <nav>
    <div class="logo">🌊 The Ripple Effect Project</div>
    <div>
      <a href="index.html">Home</a>
      <a href="about.html">About</a>
      <a href="kindness-bags.html">Kindness Bags</a>
      <a href="river-box.html">River Box</a>
      <a href="help.html">Help</a>
      <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </nav>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="emoji">💙</div>
    <h1>Kindness Bags</h1>
    <p>
      A small bag can carry more than just a few things.
      Sometimes it carries a reminder that someone cares.
    </p>
  </header>
  <!-- What Are They? -->
  <section>
    <h2>What are Kindness Bags?</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Kindness Bags are small bags put together with useful things,
      little comforts, and simple reminders of kindness.
    </p>
    <p>
      The idea isn't to create something perfect or expensive.
      It's about putting together a few things that might make someone's
      day a little easier.
    </p>
    <p>
      The contents can change depending on what is available and what
      people may need.
    </p>
  </section>
  <!-- What's Inside -->
  <section>
    <h2>What's inside?</h2>
    <p>
      There isn't one exact list. Each bag can be a little different.
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon">🧴</div>
        <h3>Personal Care</h3>
        <p>
          Simple personal care items that can be useful in everyday life.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon">🍪</div>
        <h3>Small Snacks</h3>
        <p>
          Little snacks or treats that can add something comforting
          to the bag.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon">🧦</div>
        <h3>Practical Items</h3>
        <p>
          Small, useful things that someone might genuinely need.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="icon">💌</div>
        <h3>A Little Kindness</h3>
        <p>
          Sometimes the smallest part of the bag is the part that
          means the most: a note, message, or reminder that someone cares.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- Why It Matters -->
  <section>
    <h2>Why small things matter</h2>
    <p>
      You don't always know what somebody is going through.
    </p>
    <p>
      Maybe they're having a rough week.
      Maybe money is tight.
      Maybe they're exhausted.
      Maybe they just need one small thing to remind them they're not
      completely invisible.
    </p>
    <p>
      A Kindness Bag isn't meant to fix someone's problems.
      It can't do that.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's simply one small way of saying:
      <strong>someone thought about you.</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      <p>
        That's what the Ripple Effect is about.
        Small acts don't have to solve everything to still matter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- Help -->
  <section>
    <h2>Want to help?</h2>
    <p>
      Kindness Bags can grow through donated supplies, small contributions,
      or people simply spreading the word.
    </p>
    <p>
      You don't have to do something huge.
      Even one useful item can become part of someone's bag.
    </p>
    <a href="help.html" class="button">
      See How You Can Help
    </a>
  </section>
  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer>
    <p>
      One small act. One person. One ripple at a time. 🌊
    </p>
    <p>
      The Ripple Effect Project
    </p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>